coder › Done. `toc(markdown)` is implemented in `src/toc.ts` with tests in `src/toc.test.ts`, committed as `b4933fc` on `work/main`.

**What changed**
- `src/toc.ts` — fills in the existing stub, keeping the exported `Heading` type. Implementation: splits on lines, toggles fence state on lines starting with ```` ``` ```` or `~~~`, and outside fences matches `^(#{1,6})(\s+.*)?$` — so `####### G` (seven hashes) and `#no-space` don't count, and the text is the remainder trimmed. Slugs lowercase, collapse every non-`[a-z0-9]` run to one dash, trim dashes, and deduplicate with `-2`, `-3`, … via a counter map (so `Hello, world!` and `Hello world?` correctly collide as `hello-world` / `hello-world-2`).
- `src/toc.test.ts` — 10 tests: levels 1–6 with 7 hashes rejected, space-after-`#` requirement, whitespace stripping, fenced-block exclusion, slug rules (punctuation, leading/trailing dashes, non-ASCII dropped), slug dedup for identical and merely equivalent text, empty document.

